{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_6786f9a0338d4a1c83f83b888ab1c184","id":"pg_d3a18dc260f45f98b08e2508b8f633ef","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/datasciencemonkey-coding-agents-databricks-apps-docs-deployment-md-e4a-2508b8f633ef.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c56d270e11b55db39b0b10e6c3cec490"],"title":"datasciencemonkey/coding-agents-databricks-apps/docs/deployment.md @ e4a4b216e439","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6786f9a0338d4a1c83f83b888ab1c184"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_21b9b68e5af32cc4aa2f6994ed8fa3ac75f676edddfb61d17888ab1ad785b184"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Two MCP servers are included: DeepWiki for AI-powered questions about GitHub repos, and Exa for web search and code context retrieval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_29708a732ca47d0e42992e8a3aed49d36948690333678c2fef28dbb8f10eec59"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An MCP flow lets external clients delegate tasks: coda-bridge.py proxies stdio JSON-RPC over HTTP with an injected OAuth token, returning a task_id immediately with results fetched later via coda_inbox/coda_get_result."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2c312c020563fec223ea957d5a782674ed3d3526cb81df252e4d71f61e04df94"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project lets users run Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Hermes Agent, and OpenCode in a browser, connected to their Databricks workspace with no local setup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2ddf9a5c5b57d24e74f549a9b9acc9ede7be6eef78cf78525644c0db435dedfd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Socket.IO events include join_session, terminal_input, terminal_resize, heartbeat (client-to-server) and terminal_output, session_exited, session_closed, shutting_down (server-to-client)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3075dd5a053442eb47d1c4b96c0b8558d351ce88fca42cd703b66bbe0190f936"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app exposes HTTP endpoints including /health, /api/session, /api/input, /api/output, /api/output-batch, /api/heartbeat, /api/resize, /api/upload, and /api/session/close."},{"claim_ids":["clm_42fdf7f9be53988b7c5315ad179c2dc8497052143ecc3345383f8dccf2400da3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Production Gunicorn is configured with workers=1 because PTY state is process-local, threads=16, gthread worker class, and a 60-second timeout for long-lived WebSocket connections."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44e94e09a3442196ae3fb4553bef6129319b1792183a705301111c80f374916f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app bundles 39 skills: 25 Databricks skills from ai-dev-kit (agent-bricks, genie, mlflow-eval, unity-catalog, etc.) and 14 superpowers skills (TDD, debugging, review, git-worktrees, etc.)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4becb9b86603a45185f0ea383bf043417b90860561a336fd58ffc2ef621d846f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Claude Code sessions are traced to a Databricks MLflow experiment via a Stop hook calling mlflow.claude_code.hooks.stop_hook_handler(), configured at startup by setup_mlflow.py in ~/.claude/settings.json."},{"claim_ids":["clm_53298ba9a0abf7ec97f7da1d27ca9d6c46c5f247acd4472ec722a4dc67fef2a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project has moved from a personal handle to Databricks Labs, where development continues."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8798fd54f57140e4ff9975ea5b6a227b07619d08e02fd8ff006f884b31e45a26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app is single-user: the owner is resolved via the app's service principal and Apps API, and authorization checks X-Forwarded-Email against app.creator."},{"claim_ids":["clm_99c1b2a512335f8e4253e281ce48ef508dc4af23e5435f9f692774d9013a8505"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"At startup, Gunicorn calls initialize_app(), then a background thread runs 5 sequential setup steps followed by 6 agent setups in parallel via ThreadPoolExecutor, with progress reported through /api/setup-status."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cd1c2f644b9d0529774dd95ea3a2cc97eb61e9a594bc008150c33f2d0701ebf7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repo bundles five agents: Claude Code (with 39 Databricks skills and 2 MCP servers), Codex, Gemini CLI, Hermes Agent, and OpenCode, each installed at boot."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d8b6daa8c2835a9d1e94516f0283b069346d9797da3bfcdb88e1482bf90c7738"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The stack uses Flask, Flask-SocketIO, Gunicorn, xterm.js, Python PTY, uv, Databricks SDK, Databricks AI Gateway, and MLflow; requirements.lock is hash-pinned and auto-regenerated by CI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fd10da3b8c603463d3f1abf934c6795e10ddcaeb54fde23d6078484696d9a9f7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On first terminal session the user pastes a short-lived PAT that configures all CLIs; tokens auto-rotate every 10 minutes and are not persisted across restarts by design."}],"claim_ids":["clm_21b9b68e5af32cc4aa2f6994ed8fa3ac75f676edddfb61d17888ab1ad785b184","clm_29708a732ca47d0e42992e8a3aed49d36948690333678c2fef28dbb8f10eec59","clm_2c312c020563fec223ea957d5a782674ed3d3526cb81df252e4d71f61e04df94","clm_2ddf9a5c5b57d24e74f549a9b9acc9ede7be6eef78cf78525644c0db435dedfd","clm_3075dd5a053442eb47d1c4b96c0b8558d351ce88fca42cd703b66bbe0190f936","clm_42fdf7f9be53988b7c5315ad179c2dc8497052143ecc3345383f8dccf2400da3","clm_44e94e09a3442196ae3fb4553bef6129319b1792183a705301111c80f374916f","clm_4becb9b86603a45185f0ea383bf043417b90860561a336fd58ffc2ef621d846f","clm_53298ba9a0abf7ec97f7da1d27ca9d6c46c5f247acd4472ec722a4dc67fef2a8","clm_8798fd54f57140e4ff9975ea5b6a227b07619d08e02fd8ff006f884b31e45a26","clm_99c1b2a512335f8e4253e281ce48ef508dc4af23e5435f9f692774d9013a8505","clm_cd1c2f644b9d0529774dd95ea3a2cc97eb61e9a594bc008150c33f2d0701ebf7","clm_d8b6daa8c2835a9d1e94516f0283b069346d9797da3bfcdb88e1482bf90c7738","clm_fd10da3b8c603463d3f1abf934c6795e10ddcaeb54fde23d6078484696d9a9f7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_6786f9a0338d4a1c83f83b888ab1c184","id":"pg_d9bf85f20ecd502a8cb7e24144e4d93f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/datasciencemonkey-coding-agents-databricks-apps-readme-md-e4a4b216e439-e24144e4d93f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_17b3244555c258959dfb5cd099419e4c"],"title":"datasciencemonkey/coding-agents-databricks-apps/README.md @ e4a4b216e439","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6786f9a0338d4a1c83f83b888ab1c184"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_a98a487c13681b0c3e70d6eaf29cf4d95fbcf919770ef302b9956aa51abed2ca"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An earlier design doc lists limitations including no persistence across redeploys, a 12-hour Databricks session limit, and initially no terminal resize signaling."}],"claim_ids":["clm_a98a487c13681b0c3e70d6eaf29cf4d95fbcf919770ef302b9956aa51abed2ca"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_6786f9a0338d4a1c83f83b888ab1c184","id":"pg_e4ddfbd36def5eb9abb0382194c5213a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/datasciencemonkey-coding-agents-databricks-apps-docs-plans-2026-02-02--382194c5213a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9d7249feb0c75ea989bb4cedf4d68e9f"],"title":"datasciencemonkey/coding-agents-databricks-apps/docs/plans/2026-02-02-web-terminal-design.md @ e4a4b216e439","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6786f9a0338d4a1c83f83b888ab1c184"}
